{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a824-3367-71b3-b578-b3dbe0e13bbe"},"sequence":313,"recorded_at":1780531400000621,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823"},"task_id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823","chunk":"<read-skill-result name=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nsource: bundled\nbytes_returned: 2748\nbytes_total: 2748\ntruncated: false\n</metadata>\n\nRelative paths in a skill body resolve against that skill's directory (the `skill-dir` value on its wrapper, or the parent of SKILL.md); use absolute paths in tool calls.\n\n<skill-body id=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" skill-dir=\"/Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral\">\n---\nname: durable-test-collateral\ndescription: Load the body before the first implementation edit for a bug fix or behavior change, or when the user or governing specification makes reusable tests a deliverable. It keeps the smallest focused test with the delivered project and updates coverage when behavior changes. Do not load for greenfield work unless reusable tests are explicitly required, behavior-preserving refactors, verification-only work, plan/review/explanation/documentation/formatting/generated-output-only work, explicit no-change or no-tool work, or when the user declines tests.\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Durable Test Collateral\n\nVerification is part of the delivered project when it can prevent the same\nbehavior from breaking again. Use the project&apos;s existing framework and\nconventions.\n\n## Keep the check with the project\n\nFor a bug fix or behavior change, add or update the smallest maintained test in\nthe repository&apos;s normal test layout that exercises the changed behavior. If a\nspecification makes a reusable suite or test category a deliverable, implement\nthat suite instead of treating it as private verification.\n\nAn inline interpreter command, heredoc, scratch script, temporary-directory\ntest, demo, or manual probe may help diagnose the problem, but it does not\nreplace the maintained test. Keep a useful self-authored test unless the user\nexplicitly asks for a disposable probe.\n\nDo not add a new test framework solely to satisfy this skill. If the repository\nhas no maintained harness and the request does not require one, disclose when\ndurable coverage would be disproportionate or infeasible and use the narrowest\nhonest verification instead.\n\nOn a later turn, update the maintained test even when the old suite remains\ngreen and the user does not repeat the test request. Cover the new behavior,\nnot merely an unrelated cleanup in the test file.\n\n## Prove the maintained check\n\nObserve the authentic failure before the implementation change when it is safe\nand runnable. Then make the smallest implementation change and run the focused\nmaintained test after the final relevant source or test edit.\n\nDo not weaken or delete a real failing test to obtain green. Fix the product,\nor explain why the test&apos;s expectation is wrong before changing that\nexpectation. Do not repeat an unchanged check solely to collect evidence.\n\nRun a broad or full suite only when the user, a repository gate, or\nproportionate risk requires it. A focused regression test comes first; broad\nproof does not substitute for missing focused coverage.\n\nIf the real runner is unavailable but the focused test can still be authored\nhonestly, leave the focused test in the repository and say it was not run. Do\nnot fabricate a passing result.\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5bf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a824-3367-71b3-b578-b3dbe0e13bbe"},"sequence":314,"recorded_at":1780531400000623,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823"},"task_id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0a827-0e0f-7002-8a27-3e697a7d7823"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a824-3367-71b3-b578-b3dbe0e13bbe"},"sequence":315,"recorded_at":1780531400000625,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a827-0e55-7372-84b9-2a4a361f7580"},"task_id":"01a0a827-0e55-7372-84b9-2a4a361f7580","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a827-0e55-7372-84b9-2a4a361f7580","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/references/negative-evidence.md`.\n1|# Negative Evidence Contract\n2|\n3|A passing suite means nothing unless something in it would have failed. This\n4|file is the single source of truth for the rules that make a green check mean\n5|something, and for the incident record behind each one. The operative wording\n6|that reaches every spawned child lives in the spawn template section\n7|`Evidence That Counts`; the reviewer's licence lives in `.roles/reviewer/role.md`;\n8|the repeated-variant heuristic lives in `.roles/orchestrator/role.md`. Read this\n9|file when you need the shapes, the failure vocabulary, or the incidents that\n10|produced a rule — do not restate these rules in other documents.\n11|\n12|| Rule | Operative statement | Evidence record |\n13|| --- | --- | --- |\n14|| Negative tests for gates | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n15|| Narrowing, not deleting | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n16|| Production call site | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n17|| Absence vs failure to read | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n18|| Prove, or report nothing | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n19|| Reviewer licence to defeat a gate | `.roles/reviewer/role.md` | this file |\n20|| Many variants, one unowned decision | `.roles/orchestrator/role.md` | this file |\n21|\n22|## Negative Tests For Gates\n23|\n24|Any feature that GATES, REFUSES, VALIDATES, AUTHORIZES, or ATTESTS must ship\n25|with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it is supposed to\n26|reject. A positive test proving the happy path passes is not evidence that the\n27|gate works; it is evidence that the gate is reachable.\n28|\n29|This is the dominant defect class in this repository's 2026-07-28..08-03 waves.\n30|Every instance below was found because a reviewer deliberately attacked the\n31|gate, not because anyone read the code:\n32|\n33|- the fact-assay attested a COLD child that never inherited the context, because\n34|  it checked inventory, session id, digests, and output shape, but never\n35|  inheritance;\n36|- the assay fork had repository tool access, so it could answer from disk while\n37|  the base was false;\n38|- the builder attestation accepted a correctly-shaped forged digest that the\n39|  caller minted itself;\n40|- clearance enforcement existed but no production path called it, and counting\n41|  tests around a fake proved nothing;\n42|- an unknown assay event preserved a false zero-tool observation;\n43|- a provider capability was declared absent to disable a flaky check, and the\n44|  claim did not reproduce (9/11 success).\n45|\n46|## Standard Negative Shapes\n47|\n48|Use these names in checklists, verdicts, and test names. They are the shapes a\n49|negative test must cover and the shapes a reviewer looks for first.\n50|\n51|| Shape | What it looks like when nobody tests for it | What the negative test must do |\n52|| --- | --- | --- |\n53|| Forged or self-minted evidence | The caller supplies the proof that the gate checks, and a correctly-shaped value passes. | Mint the evidence in the test the way a caller could, and require refusal. |\n54|| Absent evidence treated as satisfied | Missing input takes the permissive branch; the suite only ever supplies the input. | Remove the evidence entirely and require refusal, not a default-pass. |\n55|| Check present but uncalled from production | The guard is implemented and unit-tested by direct call; no production path invokes it. | Drive the real entry point — launch, materialize, resolve, publish — and name the production call site. |\n56|| Bypass path around the check | One entry point enforces; a second, older, or retry/renewal path does not. | Exercise every entry point that reaches the protected state, including retry, renewal, resume, and recovery, and every delivery surface that carries the rule — a contract clause reaching one context profile and not the other is this shape. |\n57|| Capability claim that does not reproduce | A capability is declared absent or present to make a flaky check go away. | Re-run the claim enough times to state a real rate, or report unknown. |\n58|\n59|## Derive Completeness From An Independent Source\n60|\n61|Completeness is derived from the pinned source or generated artifact, never\n62|enumerated by hand. When a registry, schema set, or declared scope defines the\n63|members, derive the expected set from that source and fail when any member lacks\n64|enforcement. This rule comes from five consecutive review rounds that each\n65|closed exactly the hand-picked members named by the previous reviewer; the next\n66|unlisted member defeated every list.\n67|\n68|A completeness test that reads the implementation's own table is circular and\n69|can never detect a missing entry: removing the entry also removes it from the\n70|test's expected set. Derive the expectation from the normative source of truth,\n71|not from the code under test. This distinction was what let the next Story's\n72|round-1 review demand a source-derived completeness test instead of accepting\n73|the producer's two selected cases.\n74|\n75|## Prove Exact Bounds At The Production Entry\n76|\n77|Prove every bound in both directions at the production entry: accept at the\n78|limit and refuse past the limit. Character bounds count characters rather than\n79|bytes. The motivating failure was a value containing 3,999 characters but\n80|5,999 bytes that production rejected with a byte comparison even though the\n81|normative `string[1..4096]` bound permitted it; helper-only or ASCII-only tests\n82|could not expose that narrowing.\n83|\n84|## Disable Every Refusal Clause\n85|\n86|Disable each refusal clause individually. If the suite stays green, that clause\n87|is a hole unless the test or evidence documents it as provably subsumed and\n88|names the check that subsumes it. This is measured rather than hypothetical: in\n89|one file, disabling 110 clause sites produced 45 surviving mutants, and 12 of\n90|those survivors were genuine widenings.\n91|\n92|Numeric-bound mutation and clause-disablement are different classes, and one\n93|harness rarely generates both. Numeric mutation finds off-by-one defects but\n94|cannot express disabling a tagged-union arm, cross-field equality, or grammar\n95|predicate; clause disablement finds those omissions but cannot move a numeric\n96|boundary. The 110-site clause run exposed widenings that the numeric harness\n97|could not generate, so run both classes.\n98|\n99|## Check Refusals Against The Normative Source\n100|\n101|A green test can defend a bug when it asserts a refusal that the normative\n102|source does not require. One observed test required production to reject values\n103|that the pinned specification permitted, so the suite protected the narrowing\n104|instead of detecting it. Whenever a test encodes a refusal, check that refusal\n105|against the pinned source rather than copying current behaviour into the\n106|assertion.\n107|\n108|## Eliminate Ambient Test Inputs\n109|\n110|No test may depend on ambient environment. Fixtures set explicit identity and\n111|all other values that could otherwise come from global configuration, the OS,\n112|or developer-machine state. A developer machine let Git derive an author name\n113|from the OS and passed the suite, while a CI runner with an empty GECOS field\n114|failed with `empty ident name`; only CI can catch this class, so the fixture\n115|must make its identity deterministic before CI exercises it.\n116|\n117|## Prove A Bound By Narrowing, Not By Deleting\n118|\n119|A test that removes a gate entirely proves only that the gate exists. It says\n120|nothing about whether the gate covers the right class. Restrict the gate to a\n121|narrower condition instead and require a named test to fail.\n122|\n123|Two repository incidents where a narrowed gate survived a green suite:\n124|\n125|- **BUG-260801-3kiloe F1** — the recovery successor cap was proven only by total\n126|  removal. Narrowing it to provider-limit signals left every other recoverable\n127|  failure unbounded, with the whole suite still green.\n128|- **TASK-260802-17wetr F16** — thirteen cycles later, the same shape: the\n129|  probe-lease cap survived deletion tests while the renewal path escaped it.\n130|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 1** — this contract itself. The reviewer clauses\n131|  landed in the role body and the shipped test checked the role file and the\n132|  lite template separately, so both halves were green while the composed lite\n133|  prompt carried neither. Assert on the composed production artifact, not on the\n134|  pieces it is built from.\n135|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 2** — the same contract, one level up, and the\n136|  clearest statement of the difference between the two shapes. The cycle-1 fix\n137|  did assert on the composed prompt, but it called the composition helper\n138|  directly and handed it the role, task-class filter, and profile itself.\n139|  Production builds those inputs inside the spawn entry point, so a mutant\n140|  narrowing only the real lite-reviewer routing just before composition left the\n141|  test green while an actual lite reviewer lost its gate-defeat licence. A test\n142|  that supplies the inputs is testing the helper, not the path. Obtain the\n143|  artifact the way the consumer does — here, read the prompt file recorded on\n144|  the run manifest after driving the entry point — so role resolution, the\n145|  task-class filter, and profile resolution are all under test rather than\n146|  assumed.\n147|\n148|Three traps when running the mutants themselves, all hit while proving this file:\n149|\n150|- **The mutant must be re-run with `-count=1`.** `go test` caches on package\n151|  sources; a test that reads `.roles/*.md` or any file outside its package at\n152|  runtime returns a stale cached PASS after that file is mutated. A cached green\n153|  is not a surviving mutant, it is an unexecuted test.\n154|- **A passing assertion may be satisfied by the wrong source.** Two mutants of\n155|  the producer DoD entries survived because the phrase asserted also appears,\n156|  differently worded, in the shared spawn template. Choose assertion wording\n157|  that only the intended source can supply, then narrow that source and require\n158|  the named test to fail.\n159|- **Restore the mutant from a copy, not from git.** `git checkout <file>`\n160|  restores from the index, which silently discards uncommitted work in that file\n161|  — during this task it reverted the whole cycle-2 change, not just the mutant.\n162|  Copy the file aside before mutating, restore from the copy, and verify the\n163|  restoration by diffing against it before rerunning the gates.\n164|\n165|## A Gate Publishes Its Coverage As A Ratio\n166|\n167|Prose about what a gate checks cannot distinguish 7 of 7 from 3 of 7. Every\n168|statement such a description makes is usually true — it is true of what the gate\n169|can see, and silent about what it cannot. The longer and more careful the\n170|description, the more thorough the gate looks.\n171|\n172|Report the fraction of intended targets the gate actually reaches, and assert\n173|that fraction so it reddens when a target drops out of reach. A target no mutant\n174|can redden is not covered, however elaborate the structure around it.\n175|\n176|Three defects of this exact shape, each found only once a ratio existed:\n177|\n178|- an AST call graph that recorded an edge only for a direct identifier call\n179|  covered 3 of 7 guarded functions while every pin passed; the package's real\n180|  dispatch was a function-value table, and the blind spot was invisible from\n181|  inside;\n182|- a classifier keyed on prose that a sibling gate was actively rewriting silently\n183|  dropped 8 rows, taking a suite from 107 executed subtests to 66, while its\n184|  completeness check `count == 0` reported nothing, because four is not zero;\n185|- an ownership gate that proved a symbol exists and a case is linked reported 48\n186|  sections as owned; measured against the specification, those bindings\n187|  discharged 2 of 394 normative clauses.\n188|\n189|A non-empty check on a derived set is the recurring form. `len(x) > 0` answers a\n190|different question from `len(x) == expected`, and only the second notices a\n191|narrowing.\n192|\n193|## A Blind Spot Is Not An Empty Set\n194|\n195|\"Nothing is there\" and \"nothing this checker can see\" are different facts, and\n196|only the second is a statement about the checker. Reporting the first when you\n197|mean the second converts a limitation into a clean bill of health, and the reader\n198|has no way to tell.\n199|\n200|An ownership gate scanned for uppercase RFC 2119 keywords. Sections stating their\n201|obligations in declarative present tense scored zero, were bucketed as carrying\n202|no obligations, and were admitted with no evidence required. Its documentation\n203|said \"there is no obligation to enumerate\". The true sentence was \"the section\n204|carries no keyword line, so the scanner cannot see its obligations\" — and 19 of\n205|151 headings were free-admission surface the moment they were bound, including a\n206|19-row exit-code registry and a closed manifest specification.\n207|\n208|Two rules follow:\n209|\n210|- State the bound of what the checker can see, next to what it reports. A\n211|  residual class that is named can be attacked later; one that is implied cannot.\n212|- Do not let the bucket for \"nothing to check\" also be the bucket that skips the\n213|  check. Where absence of measurable obligation is a legitimate state, require an\n214|  explicit reviewed justification for it, so the weakest entries are the ones\n215|  that must say the most rather than the least.\n216|\n217|## An Absence And A Failure To Read Are Different Facts\n218|\n219|Absence is a legitimate state with a defined fallback. A failed, partial, or\n220|malformed read is evidence of a problem. Treating the second as the first lets\n221|the fallback launder a fault into a normal-looking value, and a fallback defined\n222|for absence must never fire on a read failure.\n223|\n224|Each of these was a separate defect in this repository:\n225|\n226|- a non-empty value read as verified;\n227|- an unknown scanner version read as clean;\n228|- a partial provenance record read as absent;\n229|- a zero pid start time read as alive;\n230|- a malformed `api_error_status` read as missing;\n231|- an unparsed envelope read as no envelope — this one produced a false provider\n232|  suppression that would have hidden a healthy provider for hours.\n233|\n234|## Prove, Or Report Nothing\n235|\n236|Where a property cannot be established, report unparsed or unknown rather than\n237|inferring it from a proxy signal. A plausible guess is worse than an explicit\n238|unknown, because callers act on it.\n239|\n240|Incident: headless top-level inference in the Claude classifier was unsound in\n241|principle and produced six variants before it was deleted rather than\n242|strengthened.\n243|\n244|## Many Variants, One Unowned Decision\n245|\n246|A long run of same-shaped variants usually means a decision has more than one\n247|owner, not that there are many bugs. Eleven framing variants stopped reproducing\n248|only when structure got a single scanner and a single state type; every per-site\n249|patch before that produced the next variant. The operative wording is in\n250|`.roles/orchestrator/role.md`: unify the decision, do not patch each site.\n251|\n252|## Reviewer Licence\n253|\n254|Reviewers are explicitly licensed to attempt to defeat a gate and to reject a\n255|change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a\n256|guard is in force. The operative wording is in `.roles/reviewer/role.md`.\n257|\n258|## Exact-Evidence Reuse Is Not Full Replay\n259|\n260|A green validation result is evidence about ONE candidate: the source and test\n261|tree it ran against, the suite and configuration it ran with, and the\n262|environment it ran in. Progressive checks may reuse that exact result while\n263|all four identities are unchanged; the moment any of them differs, the result\n264|is evidence about a different candidate and a rerun is required. The runtime\n265|binding — which identities are hashed, what `reused_from_revision` records,\n266|and why an absent or malformed environment identity forces a reasoned rerun —\n267|is [docs/delivery-validation.md](../docs/delivery-validation.md). This page\n268|states the shapes a plan and a reviewer check against.\n269|\n270|- **Freeze the candidate before execution.** Evidence is bound to a captured\n271|  tree, never to \"the worktree as it is now\". A result produced while the tree\n272|  was still moving is evidence about no candidate at all.\n273|- **Full replay needs a reason.** Re-running the whole configured suite is\n274|  justified by exactly three things: a changed input identity, coverage the\n275|  reused evidence does not carry, or a recorded diagnostic reason. \"To be\n276|  safe\", \"the runbook always does\", or a retry that lost track of what already\n277|  ran are not reasons, and each burns the same budget the incident measured.\n278|- **Reuse never disarms the reviewer.** An independent reviewer retains\n279|  targeted adversarial discretion over a reused green: the attack described in\n280|  `Licence To Defeat A Gate` is against the candidate, not against the log,\n281|  and a reused result is one more input to attack, not a waiver.\n282|- **References and digests replace duplicated corpora.** A manifest of\n283|  content digests proves what was checked; a second copy of the corpus proves\n284|  only that the bytes were attached again. Portable archives are for a named\n285|  consumer that cannot resolve references, and for nothing else.\n286|\n287|## Refusal Rows: Research And Validation Budgets\n288|\n289|The rows below are what the guidance REFUSES, and the two controls are what it\n290|must keep admitting. Check a research plan, a rework brief, or a validation\n291|decision against both halves: a rule that refuses everything satisfies the\n292|first half and fails the second. Each refusal row names the observed incident\n293|behind it (`TASK-260909-2ax2l1` retrospective and addendum).\n294|\n295|| # | Scenario | Verdict | Why, and what the incident looked like |\n296|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n297|| R1 | An agent justifies a second serial research prerequisite by consistency alone — \"the sibling leaf has a gate, so this class needs one too\", \"the harness should also cover\", symmetry with a prior leaf | **Refused.** A second serial prerequisite needs a checked spec gap (`solution-architect` rule 3: the missing piece, the requirement left incomplete, the spec sections checked) and its own budget; otherwise the finding is a focused regression in the owning leaf | Three nested gate leaves (contract gate, atom shapes, codepoints) were spawned from `repeat-of:` verdicts; production coverage stayed 0/28 vectors, 0/32 guards |\n298|| R2 | Reuse of a green result after the harness, the source tree, the test tree, the configuration or the environment changed | **Refused.** Any changed identity makes the evidence about a different candidate; rerun with the diagnostic reason recorded. An earlier empty candidate never exempts a later source change | Reviewer anchors on a stale producer/revision are documented in two verdicts; a candidate was reviewed against a tree it no longer was |\n299|| R3 | A gate claimed green with logs missing, truncated, unreadable, or ending before the last command | **Refused.** A failed or partial read is not a pass and not an absence; report which commands ran, which exit codes were observed, and mark the rest unrun. A cached `ok` on a package that reads files outside its module is this row | A 20-command suite timed out at command 13 of 20 after twelve greens; the seven unrun commands are unrun, not passed |\n300|| R4 | A retry, resume, recovery or republish that starts its budgets from zero | **Refused.** Worker time, artifact bytes and serial depth accumulate across every continuation of the same leaf; a continuation inherits the budget position it was cancelled at | 13 of 42 runs were cancelled continuations; the chain re-entered full publication validation on an empty-delta research handoff until an operator directive stopped it |\n301|| C1 | An unchanged green candidate: the same frozen tree, suite, configuration and environment, presented again for a later check | **Admissible.** Reuse the exact evidence; do not replay. The reviewer may still attack the candidate | The positive control for R2 and R3: identical identities, readable digest-matching log |\n302|| C2 | A legitimate research-only Change Request with an empty `repository_delta`, whose task-scoped outcomes are attached and whose decision is recorded | **Admissible.** Publish it for independent review, skip source validation as `docs/delivery-validation.md` records, and route to the first implementation slice | The positive control for R1 and R4: one bounded contract task is the intended shape; twelve consecutive empty revisions with no consuming slice is what R1 and R4 refuse |\n303|","final_result":true}}}
