{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cde7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a824-3367-71b3-b578-b3dbe0e13bbe"},"sequence":1358,"recorded_at":1780531400002711,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"70aff3fa-2b06-43ab-b4a6-dd81d1872e01"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Release validation is ready for review (board status `to-review`, 14/14 checklist, outcome artifact attached).\n\nWhat was delivered, all uncommitted in the story worktree:\n- Test suite grew from 23 to 51, all green locally (`python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests`, exit 0): 10 new metadata-gate tests, 3 preflight tests, 7 end-to-end packaging refusal tests through the real `release.sh`, plus new docs-consistency and workflow-wiring suites.\n- `RELEASING.md` gained an exact-requirements reference table (signing identity, tag rules, build formula `run 1..9899 / attempt 1..99`, notary profile, Sparkle 2.10.0 pin + checksum, appcast invariants, generator commit, publish order), each row tied to its enforcing script. The docs tests were observed red before this update and green after.\n- 11 narrowing mutants, each admitting exactly one member of its reject class, were all killed by named tests with zero survivors — including M9, the token-preserving attack on DMG signing that the static wiring check still passes but the behavioral packaging suite catches.\n\nNo production script needed a change: every gate held. Two real coverage holes were found and closed (preflight's Developer-ID-vs-same-team requirement, and the appcast shortVersion clause). No tag was created and nothing published — `git tag` shows only the pre-existing `v1.1.0`.\n\nBounds are stated honestly in the attached `TASK-260916-2vzsmy_validation.md`: real Apple notarization, the Sparkle download path, the Swift suite/full build, and the CI run itself were not exercised in this leaf; `bash -n` + `py_compile` stood in for lint since no linter is configured.","reason":null}}
